     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Spanish speaker alert",
     "title": "Wind FROM, current TO",
     "paras": [
      "<b>Wind north-west</b> comes <b>from</b> the north-west, like <i>viento del noroeste</i>. (A current is the opposite: it is named for where it goes.)",
      "Compass points in English: <b>north, south, east, west</b>; <i>noroeste</i> = <b>north-west</b>, <i>sudeste</i> = <b>south-east</b>. North or south always comes first."
     ],
     "avoid": "west-north · the wind goes to north-west (when it comes from there)"
